COMPATIBILITY.md:207:| rebase | partial | Replayed commits keep the original author and stamp the running user as committer (a fold — `fixup`/`squash`/`amend` — keeps the target commit's author, matching Git); a missing `user.name`/`user.email` fails closed with the same identity error as `commit` rather than writing a placeholder. `--onto <newbase> [<upstream>] [<branch>]`, `--root [--onto <newbase>]` (optional positional is `<branch>`; without `--onto` the root stays parentless and unchanged picks keep their hashes), `--autosquash` / `--no-autosquash` (explicit `--autosquash` skips the already-up-to-date shortcut; last one wins; `rebase.autosquash` does not affect non-interactive rebase), explicit `--reapply-cherry-picks`, and non-interactive P1-07 controls are supported. `--autostash` / `--no-autostash` preserve tracked index/worktree changes in an fsynced held object across success, conflict, continue, skip, and abort, restoring the staged index and unstaged worktree as separate three-way layers; a restore conflict promotes the object to the normal stash list. Repeatable `--exec <cmd>` runs after each replayed commit under a required workspace-write, network-denied sandbox; non-zero/timeout stops with `LBR-CONFLICT-002`, `--continue` retries, and `--skip` keeps the applied commit while skipping its remaining exec commands. `--update-refs` / `--no-update-refs` atomically retarget other local branches in the rewritten range using captured-tip checks, including autosquash/empty/skip mappings, while excluding branches checked out in any worktree. `--fork-point` / `--no-fork-point` select the most specific upstream-reflog tip still ancestral to HEAD, with merge-base fallback. Toggle pairs are last-wins. `--rerere-autoupdate` / `--no-rerere-autoupdate` override rerere staging for the sequence, are last-wins, and persist through `--continue`; omission inherits `rerere.autoUpdate`, and both are no-ops with rerere disabled. `--keep-empty` (default no-op), `--no-keep-empt